From: Crescentm <guyues@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: drain a port's egress path on
 link down

ppe_port_mac_link_down() closes the port's bridge TX gate
(PORT_BRIDGE_CTRL.TXMAC_EN) and then tears the MAC down straight away.
Qualcomm's own switch driver does not. In qca-ssdk
qca_hppe_mac_sw_sync_task(), which is the link handler for HPPE (IPQ807x)
and also for APPE (IPQ95xx), the link-down sequence is:

  1. clear PORT_BRIDGE_CTRL.TXMAC_EN
  2. wait 10ms
  3. disable the MAC receiver
  4. XGMAC only: set MAC_RX_CONFIGURATION.LM, wait 1ms, clear it
     ("release ppe port egress packets when link down", qca-ssdk
     "enable and disable loopback for xgmac to fix qm stuck issue")

Packets that are still in a port's egress path when its link drops can
wedge the PPE queue manager for that port. The port then comes back with
its carrier up but never transmits again, and only a reboot clears it.
This was found and fixed on IPQ807x by the OpenWrt qca_ppe driver; the
IPQ9574 PPE uses the same PORT_BRIDGE_CTRL register (0x60300 + 4 * port,
TXMAC_EN bit 16) and the same Synopsys XGMAC (RX configuration at
0x500000 + (port - 1) * 0x4000 + 0x4, LM bit 10), and qca-ssdk runs the
same sequence on it.

Do the same here: wait 10ms after closing the gate, for both GMAC and
XGMAC, and on XGMAC pulse loopback for 1ms after RX is disabled and
before TX is. RX goes down first so the frames returned by the loop are
dropped rather than forwarded as ingress of the port that is going down.
The loopback is left alone if it is already set, like qca-ssdk does.

The link-up side already matches qca-ssdk: TXMAC_EN is only set again as
the last step of ppe_port_mac_link_up(), and probe only opens it on the
CPU port.

phylink calls mac_link_down() from process context (the resolve work or
phylink_stop(), with state_mutex held), and this function already sleeps
in cancel_delayed_work_sync(), so the sleeps are safe there.

Based on the OpenWrt qualcommax qca_ppe change by Julius Bairaktaris.

Link: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/24188
Link: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/lklm/qca-ssdk
Signed-off-by: Crescentm <guyues@outlook.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_port.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_port.c
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 /* PPE Port MAC initialization and PPE port MAC functions. */
 
 #include <linux/clk.h>
+#include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/of_net.h>
 #include <linux/pcs/pcs-qcom-ipq9574.h>
@@ -22,6 +23,17 @@
 /* PPE BM port start for PPE MAC ports */
 #define PPE_BM_PORT_MAC_START			7
 
+/* Time given to the PPE on link down to push out what is already past
+ * the port's bridge TX gate before the MAC is torn down. Same 10ms as
+ * qca-ssdk qca_hppe_mac_sw_sync_task().
+ */
+#define PPE_PORT_EGRESS_DRAIN_US		10000
+
+/* XGMAC loopback window used to release the MAC's egress path on link
+ * down, qca-ssdk: "1ms is enough to release all packets".
+ */
+#define PPE_PORT_XGMAC_LB_DRAIN_US		1000
+
 /* Poll interval time to poll GMAC MIBs for overflow protection,
  * the time should ensure that the 32bit GMAC packet counter
  * register would not overflow within this time at line rate
@@ -992,6 +1004,35 @@ static int ppe_port_gmac_link_down(struct ppe_port *pp
 	return regmap_clear_bits(ppe_dev->regmap, reg, GMAC_TRXEN);
 }
 
+/* Release what is still in an XGMAC port's egress path by briefly looping
+ * the transmitter back into the MAC, as qca-ssdk does on link down
+ * (adpt_hppe_port_mac_loopback_reset(), "enable and disable loopback for
+ * xgmac to fix qm stuck issue"). Packets stranded there when the link drops
+ * can wedge the PPE queue manager for that port until reboot. Must run with
+ * RX already disabled, so the looped frames are dropped instead of being
+ * forwarded as ingress of this port, and with TX still enabled, since the
+ * loop is only a way out for the queued packets while the transmitter runs.
+ */
+static int ppe_port_xgmac_egress_release(struct ppe_port *ppe_port)
+{
+	struct ppe_device *ppe_dev = ppe_port->ppe_dev;
+	u32 reg = PPE_PORT_XGMAC_ADDR(ppe_port->port_id) + XGMAC_RX_CONFIG_ADDR;
+	int ret;
+
+	/* Leave a loopback that somebody else enabled alone, like qca-ssdk */
+	ret = regmap_test_bits(ppe_dev->regmap, reg, XGMAC_LM);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret < 0 ? ret : 0;
+
+	ret = regmap_set_bits(ppe_dev->regmap, reg, XGMAC_LM);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	fsleep(PPE_PORT_XGMAC_LB_DRAIN_US);
+
+	return regmap_clear_bits(ppe_dev->regmap, reg, XGMAC_LM);
+}
+
 /* PPE port XGMAC link down configuration */
 static int ppe_port_xgmac_link_down(struct ppe_port *ppe_port)
 {
@@ -999,13 +1040,19 @@ static int ppe_port_xgmac_link_down(struct ppe_port *p
 	int ret, port = ppe_port->port_id;
 	u32 reg;
 
-	/* Disable XGMAC RX and TX */
+	/* Disable XGMAC RX */
 	reg = PPE_PORT_XGMAC_ADDR(port);
 	ret = regmap_clear_bits(ppe_dev->regmap,
 				reg + XGMAC_RX_CONFIG_ADDR, XGMAC_RXEN);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/* Release the egress path before the transmitter goes down */
+	ret = ppe_port_xgmac_egress_release(ppe_port);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	/* Disable XGMAC TX */
 	return regmap_clear_bits(ppe_dev->regmap,
 				 reg + XGMAC_TX_CONFIG_ADDR, XGMAC_TXEN);
 }
@@ -1027,6 +1074,13 @@ static void ppe_port_mac_link_down(struct phylink_conf
 	ret = regmap_clear_bits(ppe_dev->regmap, reg, PPE_PORT_BRIDGE_TXMAC_EN);
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_port_mac_link_down;
+
+	/* Let the egress path drain before the MAC goes away: packets left
+	 * there when the link drops can wedge the queue manager, so the port
+	 * gets its carrier back but never transmits again. phylink calls
+	 * mac_link_down() from process context, so sleeping is fine here.
+	 */
+	fsleep(PPE_PORT_EGRESS_DRAIN_US);
 
 	if (mac_type == PPE_MAC_TYPE_GMAC)
 		ret = ppe_port_gmac_link_down(ppe_port);
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_regs.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_regs.h
@@ -720,6 +720,7 @@
 /* XGMAC RX configuration register */
 #define XGMAC_RX_CONFIG_ADDR			0x4
 #define XGMAC_GPSL_M				GENMASK(29, 16)
+#define XGMAC_LM				BIT(10)
 #define XGMAC_WD				BIT(7)
 #define XGMAC_GPSLEN				BIT(6)
 #define XGMAC_CST				BIT(2)
